const notes=`# First report validation and dispositions

Report-1 ends with explicit Complete status and lists F1, F2 and F3. Its full claim accounting was read and checked against the complete actual draft and original source. The accounting covers the title, full standfirst, byline, lead, every subheading, all narrative sentences, all quotation clauses and the final link and reading recommendation. Pronouns' person, number and natural versus grammatical gender are accounted separately. The cited source passages and their attached modifiers preserve attribution, scope, chronology, units, conditional judgments, absent measurements, dataset exclusions and non-causal status. No faulty pairing or genuinely unresolved material claim beyond the three supported findings was detected.

F1 accepted. The actual draft says “mätte Elm Quay Housing tiden från anmälan till tilldelning av reparationsärenden”. The source says “Elm Quay's internal trial note, 4 December 2025, says that 31 repair reports were entered” and “Median time from report to assignment was two working days during the trial and three in the preceding eight-week period.” It identifies the note and statistic, not the party that measured the time. The report's external-analyst case is compatible with the supplied text. Repair: “Under ett åtta veckor långt försök i två hus prövade Elm Quay Housing en gemensam reparationslogg.” The source supports the trial, team, shared log, two buildings and eight weeks. Keeping the opening Under preserves different first words in standfirst and lead. The following note attribution and qualifications remain.

F2 accepted. The actual bridge says “arbetet inför starten”. The source says “We spent more time agreeing on the categories than entering the first reports. I would set that time aside before the next building starts.” Before the next building starts qualifies the future conditional recommendation, not the chronology of original category agreement. Repair is the exact proposed “I mejlintervjun beskriver Maya Lind arbetet med kategorierna:”. The heading itself is supported by both quoted comments about preparation and is unchanged.

F3 accepted. The actual draft attributes the checklist to Svale through “Svale Systems tillhandahåller en”. The source supplies “The optional next step is the supplied implementation checklist at https://example.invalid/svale/checklist; it is a document to read, not a consultation booking or a product trial” and names Svale as the case publisher. It does not identify the checklist's provider. A third-party document is not excluded. Repair is the smaller deletion of provider attribution, “Det finns en [checklista för införande](https://example.invalid/svale/checklist).” The original separate reading recommendation remains, preserving the distinction between the final heading's broad reading invitation and the first sentence's particular document availability.

The rest of the prose, including all three quotations, is unchanged. No translation finding was alleged. No first-report finding was rejected or disputed.

A complete current prose file draft-2.md has been saved for a fresh comparison with the full original material, without transmitting this report or these dispositions to that checker.
`;
